<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta content='text/html; charset=UTF-8' http-equiv='Content-Type' />
  <style>
    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; }
    .container { max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }
    .header { background-color: #dc2626; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; }
    .content { background-color: #f9fafb; padding: 20px; }
    .alert { background-color: #fee2e2; border-left: 4px solid #dc2626; padding: 15px; margin: 20px 0; }
    /* Amber, not red: nothing has gone wrong with the senior here — the call
       simply was not placed, and the alarm colour would misdirect. */
    .header.info { background-color: #b45309; }
    .alert.info { background-color: #fef3c7; border-left-color: #b45309; }
    .button { display: inline-block; padding: 12px 24px; background-color: #dc2626; color: #ffffff !important; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 5px; margin: 10px 5px; }
    .footer { text-align: center; padding: 20px; color: #6b7280; font-size: 12px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="header<%= " info" if @phone_failure %>">
      <h1><%= @phone_failure ? "☎️ Not reached" : "⚠️ Not marked done" %></h1>
    </div>

    <div class="content">
      <p>Hi <%= @caregiver.display_name %>,</p>

      <div class="alert<%= " info" if @phone_failure %>">
        <% if @phone_failure == :could_not_place %>
          <strong>Remindly tried to call <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %> and could not get through.</strong>
        <% elsif @phone_failure %>
          <strong>Remindly did not call <%= @senior.display_name %> about <%= @reminder.title %>.</strong>
        <% else %>
          <strong><%= @senior.display_name %> has not marked <%= @reminder.title %> as done.</strong>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <% if @scheduled_at %>
        <% if @phone_failure == :could_not_place %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %>.
            <%= pluralize(@attempts, "attempt") %> made, and not one of them
            reached the phone network. That is a fault at our end.
          </p>
        <% elsif @phone_failure == :not_attempted_in_time %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %>, and was closed
            as missed before Remindly managed to place the call. That is a fault at our end.
          </p>
        <% elsif @phone_failure == :added_after_its_time %>
          <%# Nobody was asked, so nobody failed. This row was written after the
              time it names -- almost always because a reminder was edited to a
              time that had already passed today -- and Remindly deliberately
              does not telephone about a dose whose moment went by before the
              row existed. Saying so is the difference between explaining and
              accusing. %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %>, but it was added
            to the schedule after that time had already passed — usually because the reminder
            was edited today. Remindly does not call about a time that has gone by, so
            <%= @senior.display_name %> was never asked about this one.
          </p>
        <% elsif @phone_failure %>
          <p>
            It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %>, which is outside
            the hours Remindly is allowed to place reminder calls — between
            <%= @calling_hours %> in <%= @senior.display_name %>'s own time.
          </p>
        <% else %>
          <p>It was due <%= @scheduled_at.strftime('%A, %B %d at %I:%M %p') %> and has not been marked done since.</p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>

      <%#
        The caveat that matters more than the one on the completed email. This
        notification says a button was not pressed, and the most likely
        explanation is that it was not pressed — but "did it and forgot to say
        so" is common enough that leading a caregiver straight to alarm, before
        they have picked up the phone, is the wrong default.
      %>
      <% if @phone_failure %>
        <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
          Nobody was contacted, so this says nothing about whether
          <%= @senior.display_name %> did it — only that Remindly did not ask.
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
          This means nobody pressed <strong>Done</strong> on their device. It does
          not necessarily mean it was not done — they may have done it without
          marking it.
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <div style="text-align: center; margin: 30px 0;">
        <a href="<%= @dashboard_url %>" class="button" style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none;">View <%= @senior.display_name %>'s dashboard</a>
      </div>

      <p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
        This is an automated notification from Remindly to help you keep track of <%= @senior.display_name %>'s reminders.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">
      <p>Remindly - Caregiver Coordination</p>
      <p>You're receiving this because you're a caregiver for <%= @senior.display_name %>. You can turn these off in your notification settings.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
